## 📦 Using a bundler (Webpack / Vite / Rollup)

If you prefer an ES‑module workflow instead of CDN scripts, the same code looks like this:

```js
// main.js
import maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import { PMTiles } from 'pmtiles';

// 1️⃣ Register protocol
const pmtiles = new PMTiles('data/my-data.pmtiles');
maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', (req) => pmtiles.get(req.url.replace(/^pmtiles:\/\//, '')));

// 2️⃣ Initialise map (same as above)
const map = new maplibregl.Map({ ... });

// 3️⃣ Add source & layer (same as above)
```

Then bundle with your favourite tool and serve the resulting `dist/` folder.

